<title>CHINA: Japan Ex-im bank loans $80 mln for China airport.</title>
<headline>Japan Ex-im bank loans $80 mln for China airport.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Export-Import Bank of Japan has granted an $80 million loan to China to build an airport in Fuzhou city in the eastern province of Fujian, the Economic Information Daily said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The money would be loaned to a Bank of China branch that would then re-loan the funds to the Fuzhou Changle International Airport Construction Corp in charge of the project, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The loan was the Japanese bank's first to Fujian province, it said but gave no further details.</p>
<p>-- Beijing Newsroom (8610) 6532-1921</p>
</text>
